    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f8f9568f_7bec46c6",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/uicc/IccCardProxy.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 375,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-16T20:36:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I did some digging, and it turns out there is a race here. The IccCardProxy is registered both with Phone for RadioState changes and UiccController for IccChanged.\n\nThe UiccController is also registerd with Phone for RadioState, and when it sees UNAVAILABLE it will null out the IccCards and send IccChanged, so the final state will be correct; however... in the meantime, the RadioState has already changed, which will (likely) be the first message that IccCardProxy sees (not the notification from Uicc), and without this change there will be a transient where the radio (and SIM) is unavailable and the IccCard state will be unknown. Doing this narrows the race window and may be snowing over some other problems; if not, then I\u0027m not sure why RADIO_STATE would need to be used directly. In the abstract, the IccChanged notifications from UiccController seem like they should be enough. I\u0027m not anxious to find out what\u0027s lurking behind the curtain here in 1/100000 cases when the SIM is considered \"READY\" for a few uS too long.",
      "parentUuid": "69d680ad_8d1be4f3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 375,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 375,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "71f529a1790feb70a08b92e99bcee52480bb6ca5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
