        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-05-16T20:36:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "From the following RIL enumeration, here are the possibilities:\ntypedef enum {\n    RIL_APPSTATE_UNKNOWN               \u003d 0,\n    RIL_APPSTATE_DETECTED              \u003d 1,\n    RIL_APPSTATE_PIN                   \u003d 2, /* If PIN1 or UPin is required */\n    RIL_APPSTATE_PUK                   \u003d 3, /* If PUK1 or Puk for UPin is required */\n    RIL_APPSTATE_SUBSCRIPTION_PERSO    \u003d 4, /* perso_substate should be look at\n                                               when app_state is assigned to this value */\n    RIL_APPSTATE_READY                 \u003d 5\n} RIL_AppState;\n\nBy process of elimination, APPSTATE_UNKNOWN is \"any time the app isn\u0027t loading or explicitly reporting its own state\".\n\nTo support the eSIM case where there isn\u0027t an App to load, but there is a SIM, NOT_READY is specifically intended to be the reported disambiguated state to indicate \"we have a card, but no app\". If there is an app, then NOT_READY is transient.",
      "parentUuid": "6ff9b4b8_0e189ee3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 399,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 399,
        "endChar": 48
